//why we need databse => varible lost its data when restarting
# Variables in JavaScript are stored in RAM (volatile memory), which is erased whenever the server process stops or restarts. This is why we need databases for persistent data storage.
# Databases provide durable, organized, and secure storage on disk, allowing data to remain safe and retrievable even across server restarts and machine reboots
#CRUD represents the four fundamental operations performed on persistent database storage: Create (insert), Read (fetch), Update (modify), and Delete (remove).


