Which popular library is used in Node.js to securely hash and compare user passwords?
The bcrypt (or bcryptjs) library implements salted hashing with an adaptive work factor, making it the industry standard for secure password storage in Node.js.

What is a "JSON Web Token" (JWT) commonly used for after a user logs in?
To act as a digital identity badge verifying the user on future requests
A JSON Web Token (JWT) is a cryptographically signed digital token given to the client upon login, allowing stateless authentication on subsequent API calls.

In Express.js, what is the role of an "Auth Middleware" function on a protected route?
To verify if a valid token exists before allowing access to the route
Auth middleware intercepts incoming requests to protected routes, inspects and verifies the JWT token, and only forwards the request to the controller if the token is valid.


